-- title:
--   A Γ₀(qM')-pullback separating the Gauss ring from its level conjugate
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, carrying a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq$ (Laurent series over $L$) obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the subfield of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the ratios $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of a common weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) the kernel of reduction of units along $q\mid q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and let $W_0\subseteq K$ be a valuation subring consisting exactly of those $f$ for which $f\cdot y=x$ in Laurent series over $L$ for some $x,y\in A[[T]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ (the Gauss ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Let $\tau$ assign to each element of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ an $L$-automorphism of $K$ such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$: whenever $x\in K$ has Laurent series the image of a ratio $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ (with $p_g$ of nonzero image), and $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, then $\iota$ applied coefficientwise to $\tau(\gamma)x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\,\mathrm{diag}(q,1)^{-1}\gamma^{-1}\mathrm{diag}(q,1)$ equals that of $f\mid_k\,\mathrm{diag}(q,1)^{-1}\gamma^{-1}\mathrm{diag}(q,1)$. Finally let $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $q\mid\gamma_{01}$ and $q\nmid\gamma_{10}$. Then there are a Laurent series $g$ over $L$ in the field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_0(qM')$, and an $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is $g$ with all exponents multiplied by $q$, such that it is not the case that $x\in W_0$ is equivalent to $x$ lying in the preimage of $W_0$ under $\tau(\gamma)$; that is, $x$ belongs to exactly one of $W_0$ and $\tau(\gamma)^{-1}W_0$.
--
--   The statement exhibits, on the degeneracy copy of the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-level function field inside $K$, an element separating the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ of $A$-integral $q$-expansions from its conjugate under the level automorphism attached to a $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $q\mid b$, $q\nmid c$; the congruences on $\gamma$ say that the automorphism preserves the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-floor but does not lie in the split torus, so the two valuation rings are distinct. It is used in the component analysis of the reduction, through [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_comap_gauss_ne_gauss_of_forall_mem_nonunits_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_comap_gauss_ne_gauss_of_forall_mem_nonunits_xH).
